11. The results of laboratory tests (blood routine, urine routine, blood biochemistry, blood coagulation function) are judged by clinicians as abnormal and clinically significant;
12. Those whose 12-lead ECG, physical examination or vital signs examination results are judged by clinicians as abnormal and clinically meaningful;
