Montgomery Depression Rating Scale scores on day 10 and day 90 were \<, respectively; Proportion of patients with scores of 12, ≥12, and ≥22.There are 10 items in the scale, with a total score of 60 points. The higher the score, the higher the degree of depression. MADRS \< 12 indicates no depressive symptoms, 12≤MADRS \< 22 indicates mild depression, 22≤MADRS \< 30 indicates moderate depression, and MADRS≥30 indicates severe depression.

